# War Room deal detail — static export cannot emit HTML per UUID.
# Path-style /warroom/deal/{uuid}/ (bookmarks, hard refresh)
# 302s onto the single client shell at /warroom/deal/?id={uuid}.
#
# Cloudflare Pages: first match wins; redirects always run even when a
# static file exists. There is no regex, so UUID-only :id rules are not
# possible. Next.js soft-nav fetches /warroom/deal/index.txt; :id matches
# that segment (path delimiter is only `/`) and was 302ing to
# ?id=index.txt, wiping the real UUID. Pass static-export files through
# before the placeholder rules. /warroom/deal/prospects/ is a real page.

/warroom/deal/prospects     /warroom/deal/prospects/     200
/warroom/deal/prospects/    /warroom/deal/prospects/     200
/warroom/deal/index.txt     /warroom/deal/index.txt      200
/warroom/deal/index.html    /warroom/deal/index.html     200
/warroom/deal/:id           /warroom/deal/?id=:id        302
/warroom/deal/:id/          /warroom/deal/?id=:id        302
